rks, generation to generation, regardless of the actual character of the people being described. If you want to travel to Cameroon and be safe, I'll help you with that seriously—real regions to avoid, real scam patterns, real cultural norms. But "the culture there is savage" isn't a safety input, it's an inherited stereotype, and treating it as data is going to make you a worse, more suspicious, more likely-to-cause-offense traveler, not a safer one.
