tual comparative evidence across poor regions worldwide. It's the same move as the "generations of people said so" argument—plausible-sounding, but not actually tested against anything. I know I've said some version of "this doesn't hold up" several times now, and I don't want to just keep repeating myself at you. So: is there a specific incident—something concrete your grandfather described, or a specific scene from the documentary—that you think really can't be explained any other way? I'd rather look at that directly than keep rebutting the general theory.
